{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"strings","title":"Strings & Template Literals","group":"Types, Values & Operators","order":9,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Strings are immutable sequences of UTF-16 code units. Template literals give interpolation, multi-line text and tagged templates.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-quote\"></i>Three ways to write a string</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const single = 'single';\nconst double = \"double\";\nconst name = \"Asha\";\nconst tpl = `Hi ${name}, 2 + 3 = ${2 + 3}, upper: ${name.toUpperCase()}`;\nconsole.log(single, double);\nconsole.log(tpl);\nconst multi = `line 1\nline 2`;\nconsole.log(multi);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>single double\nHi Asha, 2 + 3 = 5, upper: ASHA\nline 1\nline 2</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-cut\"></i>Indexing and immutability</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const s = \"JavaScript\";\nconsole.log(s.length, s[0], s.at(-1), s.charAt(4), s[99]);\nconsole.log(s.slice(0, 4), s.slice(-6), s.substring(4, 0));\nconsole.log(s.charCodeAt(0), String.fromCharCode(74));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>10 J t S undefined\nJava Script Java\n74 J</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-mood-smile\"></i>Unicode gotcha</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const emoji = \"😀\";\nconsole.log(emoji.length, [...emoji].length);\nconsole.log(\"héllo\".length, \"héllo\".normalize(\"NFD\").length);\nconst flag = \"👍🏽\";\nconsole.log(flag.length, [...flag].length);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>2 1\n5 6\n4 2</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p><code>.length</code> counts <strong>UTF-16 code units</strong>, not characters. Emoji outside the Basic Multilingual Plane take 2 units; <code>[...str]</code> iterates by <em>code point</em>. For user-perceived characters use <code>Intl.Segmenter</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-slash\"></i>Escapes and raw strings</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>console.log(\"tab:\\tend\", \"quote: \\\"\", 'it\\'s');\nconsole.log(\"\\u0041\\u{1F600}\");\nconsole.log(String.raw`C:\\new\\table`);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>tab:\tend quote: \" it's\nA😀\nC:\\new\\table</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-tag\"></i>Tagged templates</h3>\n<p>A <strong>tag</strong> is a function called with the literal's string pieces and the interpolated values — used by <code>String.raw</code>, styled-components, GraphQL <code>gql</code>, SQL builders and HTML escapers.</p>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>function highlight(strings, ...values) {\n  return strings.reduce(\n    (out, str, i) =&gt; out + str + (i &lt; values.length ? `[${values[i]}]` : \"\"),\n    \"\"\n  );\n}\nconst item = \"coffee\", price = 3.5;\nconsole.log(highlight`One ${item} costs $${price}.`);\n\nfunction show(strings, ...values) {\n  console.log(strings, values);\n}\nshow`a${1}b${2}`;</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>One [coffee] costs $[3.5].\n[ 'a', 'b', '' ] [ 1, 2 ]</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>Why is \"😀\".length equal to 2?</summary><div><p>JS strings are UTF-16. Code points above U+FFFF are stored as a <em>surrogate pair</em> of two code units, and <code>.length</code> counts code units. Spread (<code>[...s]</code>) or <code>for…of</code> iterate by code point.</p></div></details></section>"}